# Data Sources

OilScope combines macroeconomic, household expenditure, trade and
marketplace data to analyze India's edible-oil market from both consumer
and manufacturer perspectives.

---

## 1. Consumer Price Index (CPI)

**Source:** Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI), Government of India

**Used for:**
- Consumer price trends
- Inflation analysis
- Understanding changes in consumer price pressure

**Role in OilScope:**  
CPI provides the consumer-side price context for the edible-oil market.

**Reference:**  
[MoSPI — Consumer Price Index](https://www.mospi.gov.in/)

---

## 2. Index of Industrial Production (IIP)

**Source:** Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI), Government of India

**Used for:**
- Industry activity trends
- Oil-type level industrial activity
- 12-month average IIP
- Comparison of industry trends across oil categories

**Role in OilScope:**  
IIP is used as an indicator of industrial activity within the edible-oil
market.

**Reference:**  
[MoSPI — Index of Industrial Production](https://www.mospi.gov.in/)

---

## 3. Household Consumption Expenditure Survey (HCES)

**Source:** Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI), Government of India

**Used for:**
- Household expenditure on edible oils
- Rural vs urban consumption expenditure context

**Role in OilScope:**  
HCES provides context for understanding the importance of edible oil in
household consumption expenditure.

**Reference:**  
[MoSPI — Household Consumption Expenditure Survey](https://www.mospi.gov.in/)

---

## 4. Edible Oil Import / Trade Data

**Source:** Government of India trade and edible-oil statistics

**Used for:**
- Import volumes
- Import growth
- Composition of edible-oil imports
- Understanding India's import exposure

**Role in OilScope:**  
Trade data provides the supply-side perspective and helps assess India's
dependence on imported edible oils.

**Reference:**  
[Department of Food & Public Distribution](https://dfpd.gov.in/)

---

## 5. Amazon Marketplace Data

**Source:** Amazon India marketplace

**Used for:**
- Product and brand identification
- Observed marketplace prices
- Price per litre
- Pack-size analysis
- Brand/SKU presence
- Price-segment analysis
- Product ratings
- Review counts
- Competitive positioning

**Role in OilScope:**  
Amazon data provides a sample of consumer-facing marketplace activity and
is used to supplement the macroeconomic and industry-level datasets.

The data represents marketplace observations at the time of extraction and
does not represent the entire Indian edible-oil market.

---

## Data Integration

The datasets were integrated through a SQL Server analytical layer.

The overall data flow was:

Government Data + Trade Data + Marketplace Data
↓
SQL Server
↓
Data Validation & Transformation
↓
Business Calculations & Aggregations
↓
Analytical SQL Views
↓
Power BI

Only the analytical views required by the Power BI report were imported
into the final dashboard.

---

## Data Scope

OilScope is intended as a **market-intelligence prototype**, not a
comprehensive commercial market study.

Government datasets provide macroeconomic, industrial and household
expenditure context, while Amazon provides a point-in-time sample of
marketplace pricing, assortment and competitive positioning.

For a production-grade market intelligence system, additional sources
such as offline retail sales, multi-platform marketplace data, sales
volume, distribution data and manufacturer-level information would be
required.
